# Livewire Architecture
- Keep components thin: orchestrate only; delegate business logic to the project's actions/services layer.
- One concern per component — split when a component owns multiple independent states, workflows, or modals.
- Choose the `wire:model` binding mode deliberately: plain (deferred) by default; `.live` only when the server must react per input, always debounced; `.blur` for validate-on-exit fields.
- Every loop rendering Livewire-managed DOM requires a stable `wire:key` — model key or unique value, never the loop index.
- Communicate via dispatched events and listeners; do not reach into child component state or build deep parent-child prop chains.
- Use Form Objects for non-trivial forms; keep rules, state, and reset logic off the component class.
- `mount()` receives dependencies and initializes state — it must not contain business workflows.
- Prefer computed properties over duplicating derived state into public properties.
- Extract shared behavior into traits or the service layer, not copy-pasted component methods.
